# Spec quality checklist: <Project>
<!-- Write to docs/checklists/spec-quality.md only during an authorized checklist operation.
Check a box only with evidence from docs/spec.md. Leave UNKNOWN unchecked and record remediation. -->

- [ ] No unresolved `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` marker remains.
  Evidence: <docs/spec.md:line, or missing evidence and remediation>
- [ ] Every user story names the user, capability and intended outcome.
  Evidence: <docs/spec.md:lines and reviewer judgment>
- [ ] Every functional requirement has one stable `FR-` ID and a testable statement.
  Evidence: <requirement IDs and docs/spec.md:lines>
- [ ] Every acceptance criterion has one stable `AC-` ID and observable behavior.
  Evidence: <criterion IDs, docs/spec.md:lines and reviewer judgment>
- [ ] Success measures are measurable or explicitly identified as non-buildable business measures.
  Evidence: <SM IDs and docs/spec.md:lines>
- [ ] Assumptions, edge cases and failure behavior are explicit.
  Evidence: <docs/spec.md:lines>
- [ ] The spec states product intent without prescribing implementation or architecture.
  Evidence: <reviewed sections and any required remediation>
